silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_03_cite_as_kleisli_arrow_concrete_anchor_3 a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "CiteKleisliAnchorTypedLegRecordExample" .
silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_03_cite_as_kleisli_arrow_concrete_anchor_3 silm:hasExample "In 'CiteKleisliAnchorTypedLegRecord', the bare-symbol→anchor table grounds the abstract symbols in the Tartu-Animal-Clinic / Mittens-2026-05-18 domain story. For example, TypedLeg_record is the typed olog leg corresponding to VetRecord77: Mittens veterinary examination record from the 2024-11-01 visit. After type^Kl assigns the record sort, the typed leg has the profile: outgoing arrow lambda_rec into the Mittens cocone, no other outgoing arrows (record is a leaf in this section of the olog). The cite step itself produces only Witness_record; the subsequent type and glue arrows produce TypedLeg_record and the apex.." .
